Hey there, it's the ghoul school!

2
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:26,000
Scooby-Doo and the Ghoul School is a animation, family, tv
movie film directed by Charles August Nichols.

3
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:36,000
Scooby, Shaggy and Scrappy are on their way to a Miss Grimwood's Finishing
School for Girls, where they've been hired as gym teachers.

4
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:46,000
Once there, however, they find that not only is it actually an all-girl school of famous
monsters' daughters but there's a villainess out to enslave the girls.

5
00:25:50,000 --> 00:25:56,000
Shaggy Rogers / Mirror Monster (voice), played by Casey Kasem.

6
00:31:00,000 --> 00:31:06,000
Scooby-Doo / Scrappy-Doo (voice), played by Don Messick.

7
00:36:10,000 --> 00:36:16,000
Ms. Grimwood (voice), played by Glynis Johns.

8
00:41:20,000 --> 00:41:26,000
Sibella Dracula (voice), played by Susan Blu.

9
00:46:30,000 --> 00:46:36,000
Tanis the Mummy (voice), played by Patty Maloney.

10
00:51:40,000 --> 00:51:46,000
Elsa Frankensteen (voice), played by Pat Musick.

11
00:56:50,000 --> 00:56:56,000
Scooby-Doo and the Ghoul School is a 1988 animated comedy horror television film produced by
Hanna-Barbera for syndication as part of the Hanna-Barbera Superstars 10 series.

12
01:02:00,000 --> 01:02:06,000
It is the second full-length film in the Scooby-Doo franchise.

13
01:07:10,000 --> 01:07:16,000
The film was followed by Scooby-Doo!

14
01:12:20,000 --> 01:12:26,000
and the Reluctant Werewolf in 1988, with the five girl
ghouls making their return in the OK K.O.!

15
